Z||000000||DaveL||01-29-2001||09:00 AM||||OK, I had shifting problems with my auto tranny, that turned out the cable just needed to be readjusted. Worked fine for about 3 or 4 weeks. Them started shifting funky again. Readjusted the cable again, and it's shifting OK. I've got a new cable, but was hoping to avoid using it. Looks like the old one won't hold the adjustment. So when I take the bolt off the throttle valve cable at the transmission end, what is inside there? Is there anything I need to worry about falling into the tranny here? How hard is it to attach?||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||01-29-2001||11:50 AM||||the throttle valve cable is connected by an L-shaped "hook" - it won't fall into the tranny but you do need to reconnect it when putting on the new TV cable........||||reg||1
